{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":489155,"name":"","username":"Archit","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/57b2e6/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:04:53.671Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHow are folks using Grok Bot vs Cursor Projects? I was using Grok Bot as an orchestrator for my projects, but I’m now thinking of moving that orchestration to Cursor Projects.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot and Cursor Projects don’t seem to talk to each other to share any context. I don’t want to maintain two different sources of truth for context, decisions, discussions, etc.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf Cursor Projects are better suited for long-term, persistent projects, what is Grok Bot best for? Is it mainly one-off tasks or non-coding work? What’s the right way to think about the split between the two?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-28T04:36:31.656Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":161,"reads":35,"readers_count":34,"score":812.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171375,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-vs-cursor-projects","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":131009,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-vs-cursor-projects/171375/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":502347,"name":"xunji","username":"Picasso_shief","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/p/eb9ed0/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-28T03:11:35.499Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI have the same questions and concerns. I’m also using bots to manage the entire project, so what exactly are projects?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-28T03:11:35.499Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":16,"readers_count":15,"score":33.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":171375,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-vs-cursor-projects","display_username":"xunji","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":137688,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-vs-cursor-projects/171375/6","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":502361,"name":"Anudorannador","username":"Anudorannador","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/anudorannador/{size}/108087_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-28T04:36:25.513Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHere is my solution:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGeneral scheme (bidirectional + same-session):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCursor/Project → GrokBot\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nAlways POST the GrokBot \u003cstrong\u003eroutine webhook\u003c/strong\u003e, so the \u003cstrong\u003esame\u003c/strong\u003e GrokBot owns the work (new task or notify).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGrokBot → Cursor/Project (open once)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nPOST the Project \u003cstrong\u003eAutomation webhook\u003c/strong\u003e to start a task. Instruction/settings pin the target Project or repository. Use this to \u003cstrong\u003eopen\u003c/strong\u003e the session, not for every later round-trip.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eKeep that same Project session\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nEach Automation trigger would open a \u003cstrong\u003enew\u003c/strong\u003e session. To stay in one session, use a \u003cstrong\u003egit beat branch\u003c/strong\u003e (periodic heartbeat) while the Project waits / continues with Grok.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eContent inside that session\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cstrong\u003eTemp Git inbox\u003c/strong\u003e (handoff branch) swaps docs/artifacts for that kept-alive session. Webhooks carry pointers only.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOne line\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nGrok webhook = same bot every time; Automation webhook = open Project once; beat branch = keep that session; Git inbox = swap content inside it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/1/3/13cf092ff8031d1b96ce4c678e0d0b22116610c7.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/2PeDWCJTvHo02ElDC21kYRbrF3N.png?dl=1\" title=\"image\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/1/3/13cf092ff8031d1b96ce4c678e0d0b22116610c7_2_690x481.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"2PeDWCJTvHo02ElDC21kYRbrF3N\" width=\"690\" height=\"481\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/1/3/13cf092ff8031d1b96ce4c678e0d0b22116610c7_2_690x481.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/1/3/13cf092ff8031d1b96ce4c678e0d0b22116610c7_2_1035x721.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/1/3/13cf092ff8031d1b96ce4c678e0d0b22116610c7_2_1380x962.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"1C2029\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eimage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1606×1120 113 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eand mermaid codes:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre data-code-wrap=\"mermaid\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-mermaid\"\u003esequenceDiagram\n    participant Grok as GrokBot\n    participant Auto as Project Automation webhook\n    participant Proj as Project session\n    participant Git as GitLab handoff repo\n\n    Grok-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;Auto: POST open task (pointers only)\n    Note over Auto: Project or repo pinned in Automation\n    Auto-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;Proj: Start new session\n    Proj--\u0026gt;\u0026gt;Grok: optional ACK via Grok webhook\n\n    loop Same Project session\n        Proj-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;Git: beat branch heartbeat\n        Note over Proj,Git: keepalive - do not re-POST Automation\n        Proj-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;Git: write or read inbox branch\n        Grok-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;Git: write or read inbox branch\n        Proj-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;Grok: routine webhook notify (pointers)\n        Note over Grok,Proj: reply via inbox plus beat only\n    end\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-28T07:34:29.520Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":15,"readers_count":14,"score":23.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171375,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-vs-cursor-projects","display_username":"Anudorannador","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":4,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":115314,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-vs-cursor-projects/171375/7","reactions":[{"id":"+1","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":502372,"name":"Andrew","username":"AndrewC","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/andrewc/{size}/111447_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-28T05:24:16.696Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot usage is super limited so I was force to replace all my dev bots and just tell the Project PM bot to Use Cursor Projects.\u003cbr\u003e\nSeemed to work well with no noticeable differences.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":9,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-28T05:24:16.696Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":13,"readers_count":12,"score":2.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":171375,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-vs-cursor-projects","display_username":"Andrew","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":71220,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-vs-cursor-projects/171375/9","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":502373,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-28T05:24:45.451Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, good question. The difference really isn’t always obvious.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf I had to put it very simply, here’s how to think about the split.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCursor Projects are for longer work inside a codebase. You talk to a coordinator agent. It doesn’t write code itself, it plans, delegates work to agents, and brings results back for review. Each Project is tied to a repo, runs on Cloud Agents, and keeps shared context that builds up over time and syncs between cloud and local machines. This is for a feature with multiple PRs, a migration, a full app, or anything that lasts longer than a single chat. More details: \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/docs/agent/projects\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eProjects | Cursor Docs\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot is persistent bots, AI teammates with names, roles, and their own accumulated context. Each one runs on its own cloud computer with a browser, file system, and terminal. It’s stronger when the task goes beyond the repo, like multi-step work across apps and websites, including non-coding work. More details: \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/docs/grok-bot\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eGrok Bot | Cursor Docs\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA practical split that usually works is this. Code and anything centered around the repo goes in Projects. Orchestrating tasks that spill into other tools or services, or aren’t about code, goes in Grok Bot.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn the point that they don’t share context directly, that’s a fair callout. If there’s an update on that, I’ll post it in the thread.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/picasso_shief\"\u003e@Picasso_shief\u003c/a\u003e re your request about what Projects are, check the description above and the docs link. It explains how the coordinator and shared context work.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":10,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-28T05:24:45.451Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":15,"readers_count":14,"score":18.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171375,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-vs-cursor-projects","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://cursor.com/docs/agent/projects","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Projects | Cursor Docs","clicks":1},{"url":"https://cursor.com/docs/grok-bot","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Grok Bot | Cursor Docs","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-vs-cursor-projects/171375/10","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"ca